{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1507944-what-is-the-midnight-express-no-13-engine","id":1507944,"title":"What is the Midnight Express' no.13 engine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-10T09:55:13-07:00","id":1507944,"title":"What is the Midnight Express' no.13 engine?","content":"Maybe my search skills are just terrible, but whenever I try to look up a No.13 engine or a J.W Stillwell as described in Wr20, I get a variety of unrelated train results and a bunch of Jehovas Witnesses, plus a General JW Stilwell who died in a plane crash. Nothing about an &quot;infamous&quot; train accident which created the ghost train.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter much, but I was wondering if anybody knew what the book's talking about (maybe older editions answered it...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T13:22:08-07:00","id":1507955,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not aware of any particular real life examples of what you mentioned. If I had to guess it\u2019s probably a fictional story used to provide context to the cool image of a ghost train and using the number \u201813\u2019 to invoke relatively common superstitions which surround that number as being \u2018unlucky\u2019 or \u2018cursed\u2019 or associated with premature death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-10T16:07:07-07:00","id":1507972,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11637_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11637\" data-vbnamecard=\"11637\">Gryffon15</a> that the details of the Midnight Express are fictional. The World of Darkness setting has always blended the historical and the fictional as background elements of the setting. I am not that familiar with Wraith 20, but the original details of the Express - its personnel, engine, cars, and the history of each - were first detailed in the 1994 sourcebook, Midnight Express - one of the first sourcebooks for Wraith. Chapter One and the Appendix have all the details. Everything else are adventures using the Express as their setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}